{"id": "EUVD-2026-68104", "enisaUuid": "13e1afc8-3bb1-32e0-9609-b0d1fbbdd75f", "description": "su-exec through 0.3 fails to validate numeric user and group identifiers parsed with strtol before assigning to uid_t and gid_t, allowing truncation of out-of-range values to zero. Attackers can supply large numeric identifiers that truncate to root's identifier, causing su-exec to execute target programs with root privileges instead of intended unprivileged accounts.", "datePublished": "2026-08-29T13:47:58", "dateUpdated": "2026-09-24T14:20:31", "baseScore": 8.5, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:L/AC:L/AT:N/PR:L/UI:N/VC:H/VI:H/VA:H/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://github.com/ncopa/su-exec/blob/89c016e6e08749d583efdeda04b9f73e1218e253/su-exec.c", "https://gist.github.com/thesmartshadow/ed96e2a88643c34a247c9b7cf9e311be", "https://github.com/ncopa/su-exec", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/su-exec-through-0.3-privilege-escalation-via-numeric-user-id"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-82457", "GHSA-qpg9-jg2w-m84x"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.18, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "96d374b9-771b-3067-9651-cd3cc6da119b", "product": {"name": "su-exec", "vendor": {"name": "ncopa"}}, "product_version": "0 \u22640.3"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "e5d8f30c-ae86-39c7-8790-3e6894d20d6c", "vendor": {"name": "ncopa"}}], "isExploited": false}